' diagram-type: state-machine
@startuml
title v0002 State Registry - Team-Bound Executor Capacity State Machine

state "Executor local: available" as ExAvail
state "Executor local: full" as ExFull

[*] --> ExAvail : Executor starts\nservice identity bound to one immutable team_id\nregisters same team_id + exactly one tag\nlocally observes max_capacity and running_count

ExAvail --> ExFull : Executor local decision\nrunning_count >= max_capacity
ExFull --> ExAvail : Executor local decision\nlocal runtime terminates\nrunning_count drops

note right of ExAvail
  Executor-owned local decision.
  When available, the Executor may discover
  only created tasks matching both its
  authenticated immutable team_id and its
  single registered tag, then request approval.
  The Registry applies team + tag predicates
  before pagination and never reads capacity.
end note

note right of ExFull
  Executor-owned local decision.
  When full, the Executor stops discovery and
  approval requests. The Registry is not the
  capacity scheduler and emits no capacity-based
  rejection. Team ownership remains unchanged.
end note

note as TeamInvariant
  One-team invariant:
    Executor process and service identity belong
    to exactly one immutable team_id.
    Registration cannot omit or change team_id.
    team_name is display-only and never authority.
    Foreign task, Executor, control, environment,
    or token identifiers are rejected locally or
    receive the Registry's non-revealing 404.
end note

note as Observations
  Informational observation flow:
    Executor appends executor_events with
    executor_id NOT NULL, envelope team_id
    equal to the authenticated Executor team,
    event_id, event_type, occurred_at,
    payload, and inherited team ownership.
    In the same transaction the latest
    max_capacity and running_count are mirrored
    onto the same-team executors row.
    Observations never influence Registry
    discovery, approval, assignment, or events.
end note

note as RegistryContract
  Registry capacity responses for an otherwise
  eligible same-team, same-tag task are unchanged:
    200 approved
    409 task_already_dispatched
    non-revealing 404 for unknown/foreign id
    authorization rejection for invalid identity/tag
  No 422 executor_at_capacity response exists.
end note

@enduml
